      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Spring storms in Utah bring heavy rain, high winds, hail, and melting snow that frequently crack shingles, dent flashing, and cause interior leaks. Prompt roof inspections and proper documentation are vital for preventing costly structural rot and managing insurance claims.",
        "snippet_highlighted_words": [
          "crack shingles, dent flashing, and cause interior leaks"
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1,
          2
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Common Signs of Storm Damage"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Missing or lifted shingles: High winds tear or loosen tabs, exposing the underlayment."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Granule loss:\nHail and heavy downpours wash away protective shingle granules, which collect in gutters."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Dented metal: Flashings, vents, and gutters show pockmarks or bruising from hail impacts."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Interior leaks:\nWater stains on ceilings or dampness in the attic point to compromised roof seals."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          3,
          4,
          7,
          8
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Immediate Steps to Take"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Inspect from the ground: Look for debris, fallen branches, or damaged gutters without climbing onto an unstable roof."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Document everything:\nTake clear photos of exterior damage, dented vents, and any interior water leaks."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Mitigate further damage: Place buckets under active indoor leaks and use emergency tarps if safe."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Review official guidance:\nConsult consumer resources like the Utah Insurance Department before filing or navigating a property claim."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          5,
          6
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you'd like, share:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Your city or general area\nin Utah"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "The type of damage you suspect (hail, wind, or a fallen branch)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "I can help outline the next steps for working with local contractors or filing an insurance claim."
      }
